IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-companies-domain`

§ `Part 9 — Investigations`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 9, ss 228–246.
-- Source: SSO current version as at 07 Sep 2026.
--
-- This Part governs Ministerial power to appoint inspectors and
-- investigate company affairs. Most rules are procedural/discretionary.
-- This encoding covers the computable thresholds and penalties.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Investigation thresholds — s 232`


§§§ `s 232 — Application for investigation`

-- s 232(1)(a)(i): company with share capital —
--   200+ members or holders of >= 10% of issued shares
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 232(1)(a)"
GIVEN `number of members applying` IS A NUMBER
    , `percentage of issued shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for investigation share capital company` IF
    `number of members applying` AT LEAST 200
    OR `percentage of issued shares` AT LEAST 10

-- s 232(1)(a)(ii): debenture holders with >= 20% nominal value
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 232(1)(a)(ii)"
GIVEN `percentage of debenture nominal value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `debenture holders may apply for investigation` IF
    `percentage of debenture nominal value` AT LEAST 20

-- s 232(1)(b): company without share capital — >= 20% of members
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 232(1)(b)"
GIVEN `percentage of registered members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for investigation no share capital company` IF
    `percentage of registered members` AT LEAST 20


§§ `Suspension of proceedings — s 240`

-- s 240(1): 3-month suspension after inspector's final report
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 240(1)"
`investigation suspension months after final report` MEANS 3

-- s 240(1)(b)(ii): 3-year lookback for connected persons
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 240(1)(b)(ii)"
`investigation connected person lookback years` MEANS 3


§§ `Penalties — ss 242, 244, 245`

-- s 242(1): obstruction of investigation
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 242(1)"
`penalty for investigation obstruction` MEANS 10000
`imprisonment for investigation obstruction years` MEANS 2

-- s 244(3): failure to give ownership information
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 244(3)"
`penalty for ownership information failure` MEANS 5000
`imprisonment for ownership information failure months` MEANS 12

-- s 245(3),(4): restriction violations on shares/debentures
@ref "Companies Act 1967, s 245(3)–(4)"
`penalty for share restriction violation` MEANS 5000
`imprisonment for share restriction violation months` MEANS 12


